# Agent: efficiency and project mastery

## Tokens / responses

- Default: short, direct answers; no redundant summary, repetition, or “tutorial” paragraphs.
- Do not rewrite Payload’s general documentation at length; this repo already has `AGENTS.md` and `.cursor/rules/`. For depth, point to the relevant rule file or code.
- Large files: use `grep` / symbol search first, then a targeted `read` (offset/limit). Do not quote the entire file.
- Unless the user asks to expand, avoid long code blocks and long lists of alternative solutions.

## Where things live in this project

- Entry: `src/payload.config.ts`
- Schema: `src/collections/`, `src/globals/`, `src/access/`, `src/hooks/`
- App: `src/app/(payload)/`, `src/app/(frontend)/`
- Rules: `AGENTS.md` (Payload security and patterns); details in `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`

## After changes (only when relevant to what you touched)

- Collection/global/field schema changed: `pnpm run generate:types`
- Admin component path added or changed: `pnpm run generate:importmap`
- Typecheck: `tsc --noEmit`

## Security and Payload

- Stay aligned with `AGENTS.md` and `.cursor/rules/security-critical.mdc` for `overrideAccess`, `req` inside hooks, and access control; do not repeat the same warnings every turn in chat.
